hey this is presh talwalkar  in january 2018 lady karen brady posted  a maths puzzle on twitter with the  challenge to solve it in three minutes  after people gave their replies she then  posted the correct answer and  congratulated people who got it  but as a twist piers morgan tried to  correct her  as it turned out piers morgan is the one  who was wrong  he used his calculator to verify and  then jokingly said he got the wrong  answer because he was unaware about  baudemus and the order of operations  well piers morgan if you don't know  about bodmus and the order of operations  you need to watch mind your decisions  videos you'll learn all about them and  you'll get the correct answer to all of  these puzzles  the daily mail even covered the ordeal  and obviously i need to cover more  puzzles like this so more people can  learn about the order of operations and  how to solve these problems  so what was this puzzle she posted  it was the following mathematical  equation  so you have three minutes to figure it  out  when you're ready keep watching the  video for a solution  so there are two details you have to pay  attention to  in the third line  the equation involves three dog bones at  a time  and in the very last line there are just  two dog bones  secondly the very last line involves a  multiplication  so you have to remember to multiply and  you also have to remember the order of  operations that multiplication takes  precedence before addition  so now let's solve this problem  the first equation is that three  bulldogs equal fifteen  so that would mean we divide by three  and we get a single bulldog is equal to  5.  in the next equation we can use the  value of 5 for the bulldog and then  solve for the value of the two black and  white dots  so we have five plus two black and white  dogs is equal to thirteen  this means two black and white dogs are  equal to eight  so one black and white dog is equal to  four  next we have the equation that a black  and white dog plus a total of six dog  bones is equal to ten  so we have the value of four for the  black and white dog  we then have six dog bones and that's  equal to ten  this means six dog bones are equal to  six so a single dog bone is equal to one  we can now use the values of each of  these variables to get the correct  answer  so we have the black and white dog plus  two dog bones multiplied by the value of  the bulldog  so this will be four plus two  multiplied by five  so what does that equal  well piers morgan incorrectly did  the quantity four plus two times five he  just went from left to right and he got  six times five which is equal to thirty  this is the incorrect answer because  you're supposed to use the order of  operations according to pemdas or bodmus  you need to do multiplication before  addition  so in that case we need to do 2 times 5  first so we have 4 plus 10  and that gets us to the correct answer  of 14.  did you figure it out  thanks for watching this video please  subscribe to my channel i make videos on  math you can catch me on my blog  mindyourdecisions if you like this video  you can check out my books which are  linked in the video description and you  can support me on patreon  if you have a math topic or puzzle you  can email me presh mindyourdecisions.com  or you can catch me on social media  either at mind your decisions or at  presh talwalkar
 

